From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:20:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 243/417] DXF in the integrated environment: open without
 asking, extrude picked lines

A DXF file opens without the import-mode dialog (separate Part shapes, the
default; a choice made in the preferences stays), and so does the first part
of an assembly get grounded without asking. Picking a line of an opened 2D
drawing and extruding it used to stop with "an active body is required":
the closed outline the picked lines belong to (also over several objects,
one per line as DXF files often have) becomes the sketch of a new part,
which the tool then uses. Only shapes with solids are adopted as the base of
a new part. A file with nothing readable in it says so instead of opening an
empty document silently.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
